          <attvalue for="35" value="Greater density of orbital weapons elevates the likelihood of on‑orbit incidents or attacks that could disable surveillance/navigation satellites, prompting coastal authorities and port/state control to impose conservative transit restrictions and temporary closures that reduce chokepoint throughput." />
